    "referenceSolution": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <string>\n#include <queue>\n#include <functional>\n#include <utility>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){int R,C;cin>>R>>C;vector<string>g(R);for(auto&s:g)cin>>s;int ans=0;int dr[]={1,-1,0,0},dc[]={0,0,1,-1};for(int r=0;r<R;++r)for(int c=0;c<C;++c)if(g[r][c]=='1'){++ans;queue<pair<int,int>>q;q.push({r,c});g[r][c]='0';while(!q.empty()){auto[x,y]=q.front();q.pop();for(int k=0;k<4;++k){int a=x+dr[k],b=y+dc[k];if(a>=0&&a<R&&b>=0&&b<C&&g[a][b]=='1'){g[a][b]='0';q.push({a,b});}}}}cout<<ans<<'\\n';}\n",
    "pythonReference": "import sys\nfrom collections import deque\ndata=sys.stdin.read().split()\nrows,cols=map(int,data[:2])\ngrid=[list(row) for row in data[2:]]\nanswer=0\nfor row in range(rows):\n    for col in range(cols):\n        if grid[row][col]!='1':\n            continue\n        answer+=1\n        grid[row][col]='0'\n        queue=deque([(row,col)])\n        while queue:\n            r,c=queue.popleft()\n            for nr,nc in ((r-1,c),(r+1,c),(r,c-1),(r,c+1)):\n                if 0<=nr<rows and 0<=nc<cols and grid[nr][nc]=='1':\n                    grid[nr][nc]='0'\n                    queue.append((nr,nc))\nprint(answer)\n"
  }
